<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Equation of a curve from its gradient function</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A curve has gradient function \(\dfrac{dy}{dx} = {@fx@}\) and passes through the point \(({@x0@}, {@y0@})\).</p><p>Find the equation of the curve.</p><div>\(y =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Integrating the gradient function gives a family of curves; one known point picks out one curve from the family.</p><p>\[y = \int \left({@fx@}\right) dx = {@Fx@} + c\]</p><p>At \(({@x0@}, {@y0@})\): \({@y0@} = {@Fx0@} + c\), so \(c = {@c0@}\).</p><p>The equation of the curve is \(y = {@ta1@}\). Check: it differentiates to \({@fx@}\), and at \(x = {@x0@}\) it gives \({@y0@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_xc(ex) := if every(lambda([v], member(v, [x, c, C])), listofvars(ex)) then "" else "Use x for the variable and c for the constant of integration.";
/* Design: curve through a point. AlgEquiv, not Int (a "find c" question). [p, q, r, x0, c0]: dy/dx = p*x^2 + q*x + r. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 1, chapter 10, Exercise D questions 2 and 3. */
L: [[6,-2,2,2,-2],[-6,2,1,-1,-7],[12,-2,-3,2,4],[9,6,7,-2,2],[6,4,4,-2,3],[-6,-2,7,3,2],[-6,4,7,1,2],[-3,-6,-5,-2,8],[-3,2,2,1,8],[-3,8,7,3,5]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
pp: L[ix][1]; qq: L[ix][2]; rr: L[ix][3]; x0: L[ix][4]; c0: L[ix][5];
fx: pp*x^2+qq*x+rr;
Fx: pp/3*x^3+qq/2*x^2+rr*x;
Fx0: subst(x=x0, Fx);
y0: Fx0+c0;
ta1: Fx+c0;
/* diagnostics: point put into the gradient function; sign slip solving for c */
cw1: y0-subst(x=x0, fx);
cw2: y0+Fx0;
tw1: Fx+cw1;
tw2: Fx+cw2;]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
